\title{First default switch set of the machine: \code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect~} with a 1 MiB session cap}
\taxon{Change}
\date{2026-11-24}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{queclr}
\tag{changelog}
\tag{machine}
\tag{unreleased}
\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{commit}{695edc1}
\import{base-macros}

\p{Until now a machine engine ran the generic tier unless switches were named. The default became \code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect~}: a session survives an accept, evaluation tables only nodes that are shared, binder bodies or invariant, and lambdas and applications are checked against the expected type. The machine's own cap on a warm session is 1 MiB. Evidence: no difference from the reference engine on the 230 tests and the four corpora, where only eager-reduction declines and \code{\verb~|perf/loop-unfolded-once~} are not compared. CPU against the generic tier in one batch at a load average of 57: with one worker Init -3.5 \%, Cedar +0.4 \%, reachability -2.6 \%; with 8 workers Init -3.8 \%, Cedar -6.4 \%, Std -1.6 \%, reachability -5 \%. The module's own tests keep running with no switch.}

\p{Detail: \src{rlvm-machine/SWITCHES.md}, \src{rlvm-machine/NOTES-M6.md}. Commit \commit{695edc1}. Session: [machine speed and pipeline](ses-CVTE). Related: [the switches](design-switches), [the session cap of 1 MiB](dec-KXE1), [warm sessions](design-warm-sessions).}
